# .env.example
# Copy to ~/.config/vibebot/env (production) or .env (local docker-run).
#
# One variable per provider. Each is required to use that provider's models;
# there is no bot.conf alternative — the LLM.*ApiKey registry settings were
# removed. A key is read straight from the environment at call time, chosen
# by the provider of the model being called.
#
# Only these four providers need a key from us:
XAI_API_KEY=your-xai-key-here
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-key-here
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-key-here
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-key-here

# Local models (Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio) need no key, only the server's
# address. Pick the model with the matching prefix: ollama_chat/..., hosted_vllm/...
# or lm_studio/.... Avoid openai/... with OPENAI_API_BASE for a local server:
# it redirects every OpenAI call and sends OPENAI_API_KEY to your box.
# OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://ollama-host:11434
# HOSTED_VLLM_API_BASE=http://vllm-host:8000/v1
# LM_STUDIO_API_BASE=http://lmstudio-host:1234/v1

# Any other provider LiteLLM recognises (vertex_ai, openrouter, azure,
# bedrock, ...) still works, using that provider's own native credentials —
# Application Default Credentials, IAM, or its own environment variables —
# not one of the four above. The default imageModel
# (gemini/imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001) uses GEMINI_API_KEY above, so a
# fresh install needs nothing further.
#
# Opting into Vertex AI (not the default, but supported): ADC/IAM covers
# authentication, but LiteLLM's Vertex Imagen path separately requires the
# project and region and fails closed without them. There is no
# VERTEX_AI_API_KEY — Vertex AI does not use a bearer key from this plugin.
# VERTEXAI_PROJECT=your-gcp-project-id
# VERTEXAI_LOCATION=us-central1

# --- docker run --env-file format rules ---
# This file is consumed by `docker run --env-file`, whose parser is far
# stricter than a shell. Production loads it via vibebot.service
# (`docker run --env-file %h/.config/vibebot/env`), and a malformed file
# makes the container exit immediately; with Restart=always and no
# healthcheck that becomes a silent crashloop. Rules:
#   - NAME=value, one per line, no `export`.
#   - No quotes around the value — they become part of it literally.
#   - No trailing comments (`KEY=value # comment` includes the comment).
#   - No spaces around `=`.
#   - LF line endings (a CRLF file leaves a trailing \r in the last value).
#   - Leave a provider's line unset or empty to skip that provider; do not
#     set a variable to a placeholder like "unset" or "none".
